issues.body:
`257.lean` currently carries the open infinite-support irrationality question, plus a textbook Lambert identity and a solved divisor-count variant.

I would like to contribute the settled neighbouring facts about the same series, in one PR against this one file:

- four infinite-support families (eventually periodic, pairwise-coprime, factorial, powers of two) that give irrational sums;
- a `formal_proof` link on the existing divisor-count variant;
- finite-support period noncollapse;
- the support-restricted achievement-set measure dichotomy and geometry.

The last two need six definitions in a new `FormalConjecturesForMathlib/NumberTheory/MersenneAchievementSet.lean` (fully proved, indexed). The problem-file statements would remain `by sorry` and link proofs with `formal_proof using lean4`.

None of this proves irrationality for every infinite support. The open `erdos_257` statement is unchanged. No originality or priority claim is made.
